,"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/streamer45/streamkit/issues/31/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/greenriver/hmis-warehouse/issues/6082","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/greenriver/hmis-warehouse","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/greenriver/hmis-warehouse/issues/6082/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/greenriver/hmis-warehouse/issues/6082/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/greenriver/hmis-warehouse/issues/6082/events","html_url":"https://github.com/greenriver/hmis-warehouse/pull/6082","id":3724026881,"node_id":"PR_kwDOBV4Uf864mYk3","number":6082,"title":"CoC Performance Measurement Fixes","user":{"login":"eanders","id":1346876,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNDY4NzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1346876?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eanders","html_url":"https://github.com/eanders","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eanders/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eanders/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eanders/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eanders/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eanders/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eanders/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eanders/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eanders/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eanders/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-12-12T16:20:53Z","updated_at":"2025-12-22T21:17:04Z","closed_at":"2025-12-22T21:17:02Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/greenriver/hmis-warehouse/pulls/6082","html_url":"https://github.com/greenriver/hmis-warehouse/pull/6082","diff_url":"https://github.com/greenriver/hmis-warehouse/pull/6082.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/greenriver/hmis-warehouse/pull/6082.patch","merged_at":"2025-12-22T21:17:02Z"},"body":"## _Merging this PR_\r\n- use the squash-merge strategy for PRs targeting a release-X branch\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n[//]: # (Summarize changes and include links related issue)\r\n[//]: # (List any new dependencies or relevant ADRs)\r\n\r\nFixes a bug where project-level performance metrics were incorrectly calculated when using Static SPM data for comparison periods. Static SPM values are CoC-wide (system-level), so comparing individual project reporting values against system-wide comparison values produces misleading results.\r\n\r\n**Key Changes:**\r\n- **Bug Fix**: Disabled project-level result calculations for metrics that use Static SPM data in their goal/passed calculations (`increased_income*`, `count_of_homeless_clients_in_range`, `count_of_sheltered_homeless_clients`, `first_time_homeless_clients`). System-level calculations remain unaffected.\r\n- **Documentation**: Moved Performance Measurement Dashboard documentation from `drivers/performance_measurement/README.md` to `docs/features/coc-performance-measurement-dashboard.md` for better discoverability.\r\n- **Improvements**:\r\n  - Fixed edge case where income metrics going from 0 to a positive value weren't handled correctly\r\n  - Fixed project type filter handling\r\n  - Improved display logic by moving visibility determination to the calculation layer\r\n  - Cleaned up report list page and history table display of attributes, and added standard clone functionality\r\n  - Enhanced provider comparison functionality to better handle N/A vs. 0 \r\n\r\n## Type of change\r\n[//]: # (e.g., Bug fix, New feature, Documentation, Code clean-up, Dependency update)\r\nBug fix, Documentation, Code clean-up\r\n\r\n## Checklist before requesting review\r\n[//]: # (Remove any items that are not applicable)\r\n- [x] I have performed a self-review of my code\r\n- [x] I have run the code that is being changed under ideal conditions, and it doesn't fail\r\n- [ ] If adding a new endpoint / exposing data in a new way, I have:\r\n  - [ ] ensured the API can't leak data from other data sources\r\n  - [ ] ensured this does not introduce N+1s\r\n  - [ ] ensured permissions and visibility checks are performed in the right places\r\n- [ ] Any major architectural changes are supported by an approved ADR (Architectural Decision Record) \r\n- [x] I have updated the documentation (or not applicable)\r\n- [x] I have added spec tests (or not applicable)\r\n- [ ] I have provided testing instructions in this PR or the related issue (or not applicable)\r\n\r\n[//]: # NOTE: system tests may fail if there is no branch on the hmis-frontend that matches the Source  or Target branch of this PR. This is expected\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/greenriver/hmis-warehouse/issues/6082/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/greenriver/hmis-warehouse/issues/6082/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/parca-dev/parca/issues/5860","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/parca-dev/parca","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/parca-dev/parca/issues/5860/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/parca-dev/parca/issues/5860/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/parca-dev/parca/issues/5860/events","html_url":"https://github.com/parca-dev/parca/pull/5860","id":3280294447,"node_id":"PR_kwDOCX-EPM6hhwh5","number":5860,"title":"Fix objstore operation duration metrics by upgrading thanos-io/objstore","user":{"login":"secfree","id":7149512,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDk1MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7149512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/secfree","html_url":"https://github.com/secfree","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secfree/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secfree/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secfree/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secfree/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secfree/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secfree/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secfree/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secfree/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/secfree/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-07-31T12:34:38Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T11:11:46Z","closed_at":"2025-08-18T11:11:46Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/parca-dev/parca/pulls/5860","html_url":"https://github.com/parca-dev/parca/pull/5860","diff_url":"https://github.com/parca-dev/parca/pull/5860.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/parca-dev/parca/pull/5860.patch","merged_at":"2025-08-18T11:11:46Z"},"body":"### Problem\r\n\r\nThe `objstore_bucket_operation_duration_seconds` metric was reporting extremely high and incorrect values, indicating severe performance issues that don't reflect actual operation times.\r\n\r\nBefore the fix:\r\n\r\n```\r\nobjstore_bucket_operation_duration_seconds_sum{bucket=\"xxx\",operation=\"get\"} 1.0440258375572279e+10\r\nobjstore_bucket_operation_duration_seconds_count{bucket=\"xxx\",operation=\"get\"} 2068\r\n```\r\n- Average operation time: ~5,048,480 seconds (~58 days per operation)\r\n- This clearly incorrect metric made it impossible to monitor actual object storage performance\r\n\r\n### Root Cause\r\n\r\nThe issue was caused by a bug in the `github.com/thanos-io/objstore` library's metrics collection logic, where operation durations were being incorrectly calculated or accumulated.\r\n\r\n### Solution\r\n\r\nUpdated `github.com/thanos-io/objstore` dependency from `v0.0.0-20240913165201-fd105025a2e5` to `v0.0.0-20241028145108-31c0873d5266` to include the fix from [objstore commit 31c0873d](https://github.com/thanos-io/objstore/commit/31c0873d5266a6c58fe8fb5d6de01b66dcd50f5f).\r\n\r\nCode changes required:\r\n- Updated dependency version in `go.mod` and `go.sum`\r\n- Updated `client.NewBucket()` calls to accommodate API changes by adding the new fourth parameter (set to `nil`)\r\n\r\n### Verification\r\n\r\nAfter the fix:\r\n\r\n```\r\nobjstore_bucket_operation_duration_seconds_sum{bucket=\"xxx\",operation=\"get\"} 318.43996360699987\r\nobjstore_bucket_operation_duration_seconds_count{bucket=\"xxx\",operation=\"get\"} 541\r\n```\r\n- Average operation time: ~0.59 seconds per operation\r\n- Metrics now accurately reflect actual object storage performance\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/parca-dev/parca/issues/5860/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/parca-dev/parca/issues/5860/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness/issues/3035","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness/issues/3035/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness/issues/3035/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness/issues/3035/events","html_url":"https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness/pull/3035","id":3110508671,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEVbsCM6YpO0v","number":3035,"title":" [Fix] acc_mutual_info metric calculation bug","user":{"login":"baberabb","id":92168766,"node_id":"U_kgDOBX5iPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92168766?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/baberabb","html_url":"https://github.com/baberabb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baberabb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baberabb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baberabb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baberabb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baberabb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baberabb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baberabb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baberabb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baberabb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-06-02T14:46:05Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T12:32:17Z","closed_at":"2025-06-03T12:32:15Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness/pulls/3035","html_url":"https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness/pull/3035","diff_url":"https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness/pull/3035.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness/pull/3035.patch","merged_at":"2025-06-03T12:32:15Z"},"body":"When using `acc_mutual_info`, all other metrics (acc, acc_norm, etc.) were being calculated incorrectly, as we were incorrectly slicing the results array, assuming conditional and unconditional loglikelihoods were interleaved when they're actually sequential.\r\n\r\n  Changes:\r\n  - Fixed array slicing in process_results() to correctly separate conditional and unconditional loglikelihoods\r\n  - Added missing `target_delimiter` to unconditional continuation requests (the same as original ones)\r\n\r\n  Before:\r\n```python\r\n  lls_unconditional = lls[1::2]  # Wrong: every other element\r\n  lls = lls[::2]                 # Wrong: every other element\r\n```\r\n  After:\r\n```python\r\n  lls_unconditional = lls[len(choices):]  # Correct: second half\r\n  lls = lls[:len(choices)]                # Correct: first half\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis matches how `construct_requests()` actually builds the arguments list - original loglikelihoods first, then unconditional ones appended at the end.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness/issues/3035/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness/issues/3035/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masteryachty/gpu-charts/issues/39","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masteryachty/gpu-charts","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masteryachty/gpu-charts/issues/39/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masteryachty/gpu-charts/issues/39/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masteryachty/gpu-charts/issues/39/events","html_url":"https://github.com/masteryachty/gpu-charts/pull/39","id":3288575163,"node_id":"PR_kwDOOyxV0s6h9TsN","number":39,"title":"Fix Y range calculation when switching presets","user":{"login":"masteryachty","id":184930150,"node_id":"U_kgDOCwXPZg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184930150?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masteryachty","html_url":"https://github.com/masteryachty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masteryachty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masteryachty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masteryachty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masteryachty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masteryachty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masteryachty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masteryachty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masteryachty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masteryachty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-08-04T08:47:42Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T08:54:25Z","closed_at":"2025-08-04T08:54:25Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masteryachty/gpu-charts/pulls/39","html_url":"https://github.com/masteryachty/gpu-charts/pull/39","diff_url":"https://github.com/masteryachty/gpu-charts/pull/39.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/masteryachty/gpu-charts/pull/39.patch","merged_at":"2025-08-04T08:54:25Z"},"body":"## Summary\n- Fixed Y range calculation to only include visible metrics from the current preset\n- Resolved issue where candlestick view was using incorrect Y range due to metrics from previous presets\n- Improved preset switching behavior to clear old data and prevent data mixing\n\n## Problem\nWhen switching between Market Data and Candlestick presets, the Y range was being calculated incorrectly because:\n1. All metrics were being created with `visible=true` regardless of preset settings\n2. Data from previous presets was not cleared when switching\n3. The Y range calculation included all visible metrics from all data groups\n\n## Solution\n1. **Respect preset visibility**: Added methods to create metrics with specified visibility based on preset configuration\n2. **Clear data on preset change**: Modified `set_preset_and_symbol` to detect preset changes and clear all data groups\n3. **Fix candlestick data**: Updated candlestick preset to use TRADES data instead of non-existent OHLC columns\n4. **Automatic timeframe selection**: Implemented smart candlestick timeframe selection (target 300 candles)\n\n## Changes\n- Added `add_metric_to_group_with_visibility()` and `add_computed_metric_to_group_with_visibility()` methods\n- Updated data loading to respect visibility settings from presets\n- Clear GPU bounds and pending operations when switching presets\n- Fixed candlestick preset configuration\n- Cleaned up debug logging\n\n## Test Plan\n✅ Start with Market Data preset - verify only Mid price line is visible\n✅ Switch to Candlestick preset - verify Y range adjusts to price data only\n✅ Switch back to Market Data - verify Y range returns to Mid price range\n✅ Candlesticks automatically select appropriate timeframe based on zoom level\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masteryachty/gpu-charts/issues/39/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/masteryachty/gpu-charts/issues/39/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AdJadoon/data/issues/590","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AdJadoon/data","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AdJadoon/data/issues/590/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AdJadoon/data/issues/590/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AdJadoon/data/issues/590/events","html_url":"https://github.com/AdJadoon/data/p